[size=5][b]Galactic Grand Prix[/b][/size]
[i]Kart-racer-style cups for STAR WARS: Galactic Racer - race back to back, score points, win trophies. Offline only.[/i]

The campaign is great, but sometimes you just want to race. Galactic Grand Prix adds a [b]GRAND PRIX[/b] tab to the main menu: pick a league and a cup, and race four tracks in a row against the full field, with points after every race and a trophy at the end.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Three leagues, three styles[/b]
[list]
[*][b]JUNKER[/b] - scrapyard junk with too much engine: afterburner and ramjet at 10 on a stock chassis, grimy cars, one ability, no tune-ups
[*][b]CHALLENGER[/b] - every part at level 7, yours and theirs: two abilities, one tune-up
[*][b]ACE[/b] - the finest vehicles money can buy, every part at level 10: three abilities, two tune-ups, and a field that is faster and meaner
[/list]
[*][b]Random cups[/b] - each planet's cup (Jakku, Lantaana, Ando Prime, Crait, Sentinel I) draws four races from that planet's tracks, directions and conditions (night, wet, snow, scorching, mines, storm). Plus the Galactic Cup across planets.
[*][b]The Rally Cup[/b] - every point-to-point road as a seven-stage rally in tour order: four cars, standings by total time, the night and weather of each stage drawn at the start and kept secret until it loads, the finale at night.
[*][b]PODRACING[/b] - a league of its own: the PODRACER CUP, four races on the pod tracks of Mos Espa, Mawhonic and Holdfast's Folly, against Sebulba, the other pod racers and Kestar Bool. Fly the podracer of Shade, Goli, Fola, Sebulba or (once you've beaten him) Kestar. Two levels, each with its own trophy and records: [b]LEARNER[/b] (no abilities, the pace to learn the tracks) and [b]PRO[/b] (every pod at level 7, your four abilities on your pod, and every pod racer carries a kit of their own).
[*][b]Points and trophies[/b] - 15-12-10-9...1 after every race, the standings right on the results screen, then straight into the next race. Gold, silver, bronze, a crown for a perfect cup, track and lap records with "near miss" call-outs, and the CUP RESULT on the game's own tour-end screen.
[*][b]PREVIOUS BEST LAP[/b] - your lap record on this track shown through the start countdown; your best lap on every standings.
[*][b]The Galactic Cup finale[/b] - take a trophy in the Galactic Cup and Kestar Bool waits as its fifth race: a 1 v 1 in the stadium for the league title. Beat him at ACE and he races for you.
[*][b]Rivals that stay rivals[/b] - the elite pilots drive stronger cars and are usually the ones fighting you for the cup. The bots use their abilities, and the racers ahead of you don't fire their ramjet just because you did: boosting feels fast. A lead you build is yours.
[*][b]Your loadout[/b] - pick your pilot (their face on the tile), then any of the three vehicles: a pilot's own vehicle looks as the game built it, the other two wear that rider's scheme. Each pilot starts with their signature abilities; change them and your tune-ups on each cup's start screen.
[*][b]Safe for your campaign[/b] - its own save file; everything it changes in the game is in memory only and put back at the main menu.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]STAR WARS: Galactic Racer (Steam, PC)
[*]UE4SS for Galactic Racer ("Galactic Racer Edition", Open Beta v0.9.4 or later): https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarsgalacticracer/mods/2
[/list]

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install UE4SS (it goes in [i]Griffin\Binaries\Win64[/i]).
[*]Unzip into [i]Griffin\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods\[/i] - you should have [i]Mods\GalacticGrandPrix\Scripts\main.lua[/i].
[*]Start the game: the GRAND PRIX tab is on the main menu (or press F6).
[/list]

[size=4][color=#ff6666][b]Multiplayer[/b][/color][/size]
This mod is for [b]offline play[/b]. It won't run its races while you're in a party or matchmaking, but for online play the safest thing is to switch mods off completely: rename [i]Griffin\Binaries\Win64\dwmapi.dll[/i] to [i]dwmapi.dll.off[/i], and back afterwards. Using mods online is at your own risk.

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]
In [i]Scripts\config.lua[/i] (copy it first): open the tab at start-up ([i]BootToGrandPrix[/i]), the menu key, how much stronger each pilot tier is per league ([i]AI.Strength[/i]), the Junker look ([i]Looks[/i]).

[size=4][b]Bug reports[/b][/size]
Please attach [i]Mods\GalacticGrandPrix\grandprix.log[/i] and say what you were doing. English only for now; tested at 4K.

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Delete the [i]GalacticGrandPrix[/i] folder.

